      "data": {
        "text": "**Constructing The Foundation**\n\nOkay, I've just finished the initial setup. I've got the `describe_image.py` file in place. It now includes the essential imports for Google Cloud Vision and the OS. I've also defined the main `describe_image` function, which accepts an `image_path` as its argument and initializes the `vision.ImageAnnotatorClient()`. I'm ready to move onto the next step!\n\n\n**Finalizing The Implementation**\n\nI've integrated the image processing logic within `describe_image.py`. The function now reads the image, calls `label_detection`, and forms a description. It handles cases with or without labels. There's a `if __name__ == \"__main__\":` block with a placeholder image path. Also, I've left helpful comments about Google Cloud credentials. It's now complete!\n\n\n",
